permill":{"duration":0.037439,"end_time":"2026-09-26T08:06:42.048007+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-26T08:06:42.010568+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["def load_gt_boxes(label_path, width, height):\n","\n","    boxes = []\n","\n","    if not label_path.exists():\n","        return boxes\n","\n","    with open(label_path, \"r\") as f:\n","\n","        for line in f:\n","            values = line.strip().split()\n","\n","            if len(values) != 5:\n","                continue\n","\n","            _, xc, yc, bw, bh = map(float, values)\n","\n","            # YOLO normalized -> pixels\n","            xc *= width\n","            yc *= height\n","            bw *= width\n","            bh *= height\n","\n","            x1 = xc - bw / 2\n","            y1 = yc - bh / 2\n","            x2 = xc + bw / 2\n","            y2 = yc + bh / 2\n","\n","            # Keep inside image\n","            x1 = max(0, x1)\n","            y1 = max(0, y1)\n","            x2 = min(width - 1, x2)\n","            y2 = min(height - 1, y2)\n","\n","            boxes.append((x1, y1, x2, y2))\n","\n","    return boxes"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"1b260277","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.027983,"end_time":"2026-09-26T08:06:42.107474+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-26T08:06:42.079491+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["**`loadmat(...)` in your ShanghaiTech dataset**\n","\n","Loads a MATLAB .mat file. For ShanghaiTech, the .mat file contains head-point annotations, `GT` represents one point per person, not a bounding box.\n","\n","**`load_gt_boxes(...)`**\n","It is for YOLO-format .txt annotation files\n","\n","**Main difference**\n","\n","| Feature | `loadmat` | `load_gt_boxes` |\n","|---|---|---|\n","| Annotation file | `.mat` | `.txt` |\n","| Format | MATLAB | YOLO |\n","| Annotation | Person/head points | Person bounding boxes |\n","| Example | `(250, 300)` | `(200, 250, 300, 450)` |\n","| Output | Array of points | List of boxes |\n","| Used for | Crowd density/counting | Object detection |\n","| Gives object size? | ❌ No | ✅ Yes |\n","| Gives class? | Usually no useful class ID | ✅ Yes, via YOLO class ID |\n","| Directly usable for density map? | ✅ Yes | ❌ Not directly |\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":24,"id":"446ebfcb","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-26T08:06:42.166081Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-26T08:06:42.165426Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-26T08:06:42.171627Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-26T08:06:42.170766Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.038289,"end_time":"2026-09-26T08:06:42.173394+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-26T08:06:42.135105+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["def predict_fourcolumn_mcnn(image_path):\n","    image_bgr = cv2.imread(str(image_path))\n","\n","    if image_bgr is None:\n","        raise ValueError(f\"Could not read image: {image_path}\")\n","\n","    # RGB copy for visualization\n","    original_image = cv2.cvtColor(image_bgr, cv2.COLOR_BGR2RGB)\n","\n","    # RESIZE EXACTLY LIKE TRAINING\n","    resized_image = cv2.resize(original_image, (768, 768))\n","    \n","    # CONVERT TO PYTORCH TENSOR\n","    input_tensor = torch.from_numpy(resized_image.transpose(2, 0, 1)).float() / 255.0\n","        \n","    # Add batch dimension\n","    input_tensor = input_tensor.unsqueeze(0)\n","    \n","    # Move to device\n","    input_tensor = input_tensor.to(DEVICE, non_blocking=True)\n","    \n","    # INFERENCE\n","    model.eval()\n","    \n","    with torch.inference_mode():\n","        prediction = model(input_tensor)\n","\n","    density_map = prediction.squeeze().cpu().numpy()\n","\n","    # COUNT\n","    predicted_count = float(np.sum(density_map))\n","    \n","    return (original_image, resized_image, density_map, predicted_count)"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"1d6c40ff","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.028187,"end_time":"2026-09-26T08:06:42.23138+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-26T08:06:42.203193+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["### Convert the image to a PyTorch tensor\n","\n","The original image has shape:\n","```\n","H × W × C\n","768 × 768 × 3\n","```\n","PyTorch expects image tensors in:\n","```\n","C × H × W\n","3 × 768 × 768\n","```\n","\n","### Add the batch dimension\n","\n","Before:\n","```\n","[3, 768, 768]\n","```\n","After:\n","```\n","[1, 3, 768, 768]\n","```\n","\n","The `1` represents the batch size.\n","\n","So you're giving the model one image.\n","\n","\n","### Evaluation Mode\n","\n","This tells PyTorch that you're doing inference, not training.\n","\n","It is important for layers such as:\n","\n","* Dropout\n","* Batch Normalization\n","\n","because their behavior differs between training and evaluation.\n","\n","### Disable gradient calculation\n","\n","Since you aren't training the model, you don't need gradients.\n","\n","This reduces memory usage and makes inference more efficient.\n","\n","\n","### Extract the density map\n","\n","Suppose the model produces:\n","```\n","[1, 1, 192, 192]\n","```\n","`squeeze()` removes the unnecessary dimensions:\n","```\n","[192, 192]\n","```\n","\n","**Why `.cpu()` at the end?**  \n","\n","Because NumPy cannot directly work with a CUDA tensor.\n","\n","This would fail if prediction is on GPU"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":25,"id":"f2dc24a7","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-26T08:06:42.290753Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-26T08:06:42.290538Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-26T08:06:42.584765Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-26T08:06:42.583954Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.325682,"end_time":"2026-09-26T08:06:42.586334+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-26T08:06:42.260652+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Dataset downloaded to: /kaggle/input/datasets/masum1834e/public-transport-crowd-counting\n"]}],"source":["import 